<title>FRANCE: France ready to freeze spending to meet EMU goals.</title>
<headline>France ready to freeze spending to meet EMU goals.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Wednesday he was prepared to freeze spending lines in the 1997 budget as a precaution against overshooting deficit targets France needs to hit to take part in a single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;We have prepared a proposal for a freeze,&quot; Arthuis told reporters.</p>
<p>He declined to say how many francs he proposed to freeze, but said the amount &quot;reflected wisdom and caution&quot;.</p>
<p>Arthuis said he had sent Prime Minister Alain Juppe the proposal for a final decision as to whether spending freezes were necessary.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
